# Mutation cases for "a sce-static document lowers for the Interpreter"
# (docs/SCE_ACCEPTED_SUBSET.md §2.15).
#
# Run with
# `scripts/mutate sce-build/tests/mutations/a_static_datamodel_lowers_for_the_interpreter.cases`.
#
# The Interpreter replays the scenarios the generated backends replay, on the
# documents `sce-codegen lower` makes of the fixtures, and what it cannot lower it
# refuses by name and leaves out of the replay. A refusal that grows back therefore
# leaves the replay green with a fixture silently missing from it, so the scan this
# test makes of every fixture holds, by name, the two that send themselves their
# `<param>`s: `static_send_params` and `static_wire_enum`.
#
# Each case below puts one of those refusals back and must make the scan red.
#
# ⚠ A mutated tree is built under `-D warnings`: a case keeps every binding it had
# in use, so that it is a verdict and not an unused-variable error that leaves the
# tree uncompiled and the result INCONCLUSIVE.
#
# Anchors are literal slices of the source; an edit that moves one is reported
# INCONCLUSIVE with the anchor quoted, never as a pass.

mutation_tests -p sce-build --test a_static_datamodel_lowers_for_the_interpreter
mutation_targets sce-build/src/forge/static_js.rs
mutation_oracles sce-build/tests/a_static_datamodel_lowers_for_the_interpreter.rs

# A `<send>` that carries a `<param>` is refused again, as it was before the
# pairs were lowered: both fixtures leave the replay.
mutation_case "a send's params are refused" <<'PY'
edit("sce-build/src/forge/static_js.rs",
     "        \"send\" if !action.contentexpr.is_empty() => {\n            Some(\"a <send> that carries <content expr>\".to_string())\n        }\n",
     "        \"send\" if !action.params.is_empty() || !action.contentexpr.is_empty() => {\n            Some(\"a <send> that carries <param> or <content expr>\".to_string())\n        }\n")
PY

# An enum value has no name to cross as: a `<param>` that holds one is refused by
# the walk, and the fixture that sends one leaves the replay.
mutation_case "an enum value has no wire name" <<'PY'
edit("sce-build/src/forge/static_js.rs",
     "    fn enum_wire_name(&self, _alias: &str, value: &str) -> Option<String> {\n        Some(value.to_string())\n    }\n",
     "    fn enum_wire_name(&self, _alias: &str, _value: &str) -> Option<String> {\n        None\n    }\n")
PY
